    "architecture": "aarch64",
    "context": "Native seeded getrandom signal interruption:336 root/UID1000 controls per architecture;48 unblocked one-shot SIGALRM8MiB calls,48 already pending blocked signals,240 small zero/1/32/255/256-byte requests; six accepted flags, actual musl and raw upper-word calls, SA_RESTART on/off. Unblocked large calls must return a positive native-page multiple below the request, with the identical result in the delivered signal frame, one handler and untouched bytes beyond the reported prefix. Original kernels fail48 each by completing all8MiB; corrected and identical-ELF Linux6.12.51 zero. Existing signal masks are honored and small requests stay complete. Two warmed200-cycle page+1 blocked-signal paths measure all slabs/largepages; four completed production builds, runtime/randomrange regressions, unchanged allocation diagnostics, pinned compiler and64-input inventories, whole-C single-function scope and executing audit negatives. First pending-only candidate ARM48 failures and x86 pass are retained. Missing shared ARM SDK caused three preboot compile refusals; final ARM runs explicitly replay frozen source/C/object/ELF bytes rather than claiming a fresh C compilation. Only a borrowed-thread signal/must-exit query, loop break and cooperative scheduling between pages are added; no ownership, erasure, allocation or free changes. Entropy quality, unseeded readiness/blocking, exact signal scheduling, default stop/kill dispositions, ignored signals, thread-group-exit races, full2GiB calls and GNU/translated/ELF32 paths remain unqualified.",
